Each space class of the Vehicle, RV & Boat Parking Agreement carries the features listed for it in the class specification, and only those:

- a roof canopy where the class is covered;
- a fully enclosed garage with its own door where the class is enclosed;
- a 30-amp battery-maintenance outlet where the class includes the electric hookup;
- use of the RV dump station and the wash bay where the class includes dump station and wash bay access;
- gate access during the access hours of the class.

**A feature the class lacks.** A tenant who wants a feature their class lacks is offered a space of a class that has it, as a new agreement. Parking agreements are not transferred between spaces.

### Basis Q&A

- *A tenant in an uncovered class asks for a roof canopy.* The roof canopy comes only with a covered class; the tenant is offered a space of a covered class as a new agreement, and the existing agreement is not moved to that space.
- *A tenant asks for gate access outside the hours of the class.* Gate access follows the access hours of the class; a class with longer access hours is offered as a new agreement.

Hypothetical illustration: a tenant holding a Bluegate Uncovered RV & Boat Space (up to 30 ft) who wants a battery-maintenance outlet may be offered a space in a class that includes the outlet, under a new Vehicle, RV & Boat Parking Agreement.
